Key insight: `SplitModeView` subscribes to `editor.on('change', forceUpdate)` and re-invokes `editor.renderPreview(...)` on every change. So my preview component re-mounts/re-renders each change; inside it I can just compute the HTML. But since `renderPreview` returns a ReactNode that gets re-rendered on each change, the `SplitModePreview` component itself will receive a new render each time. The guide's pattern with debounce + `useEffect` on every render works: each forceUpdate re-calls renderPreview → my component re-renders → effect runs → debounced transform updates html state.

Simplest robust approach for my preview component:

```tsx
function SplitModePreview({getValue, md}: RenderPreviewParams) {
  const [html, setHtml] = useState('');
  useEffect(() => {
    const id = setTimeout(() => {
      const res = transform(getValue(), {
        allowHTML: md.html,
        breaks: md.breaks,
        linkify: md.linkify,
        needToSanitizeHtml: true,
      });
      setHtml(res.result.html);
    }, 200);
    return () => clearTimeout(id);
  }); // run on every render
  return <YfmStaticView html={html} noListReset className={b('preview')} />;
}
```

Wait — what does `transform` return? `@diplodoc/transform` default export: `transform(content, options)` returns `{result: {html, meta}, logs}`. The guide used `transform(getValue(), {...}).result` then `res.html`, `res.meta`. Options in the guide: `allowHTML, breaks, plugins, linkify, linkifyTlds, needToSanitizeHtml`. Hmm — the guide destructures `plugins` from props (that was an older API where RenderPreviewParams included plugins). The installed `RenderPreviewParams` = `{getValue, mode, md, directiveSyntax}` — no `plugins`. So pass options from `md` only. Let me verify transform's option names in the installed @diplodoc/transform types.

Also `needToSanitizeHtml` — verify it's a valid option.

Also check the transform export style: `export = transform` — so with ESM/TS `import transform from '@diplodoc/transform'` works with esModuleInterop. Check tsconfig for esModuleInterop.

Let me check the transform d.ts signature.

